        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<div class=\"graphic\"><img src=\"/graphics/2fe269e0903e6513fefb885d0c15c07b\"></div><p>Find the value of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: x.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "[IMG: /graphics/2fe269e0903e6513fefb885d0c15c07b]\n\nFind the value of [MATH: x.]",
            "images": [
              {
                "src": "/graphics/2fe269e0903e6513fefb885d0c15c07b",
                "alt": ""
              }
            ],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Notice that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\triangle{ABC}]</span> is inscribed in the circle, where the side <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\overline{AB}]</span> is a diameter. Therefore, by Thales&#x27; theorem, we have\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: m\\angle{ACB}=90^\\circ.]</span> </p><p>Now, using the fact that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\triangle{ABC}]</span> is a right triangle, we obtain</p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: m\u2220BAC + m\u2220ABC|= 90^{\u2218}; (2x) + (2x + 10^{\u2218})|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x + 10^{\u2218}|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x|= 80^{\u2218}; x|= 20^{\u2218}.]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Notice that [MATH: \\triangle{ABC}] is inscribed in the circle, where the side [MATH: \\overline{AB}] is a diameter. Therefore, by Thales' theorem, we have\n[MATH: m\\angle{ACB}=90^\\circ.]\n\nNow, using the fact that [MATH: \\triangle{ABC}] is a right triangle, we obtain\n\n[MATH: m\u2220BAC + m\u2220ABC|= 90^{\u2218}; (2x) + (2x + 10^{\u2218})|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x + 10^{\u2218}|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x|= 80^{\u2218}; x|= 20^{\u2218}.]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [
          {
            "src": "/graphics/2fe269e0903e6513fefb885d0c15c07b",
            "alt": ""
          }
        ],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\n[IMG: /graphics/2fe269e0903e6513fefb885d0c15c07b]\n\nFind the value of [MATH: x.]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nNotice that [MATH: \\triangle{ABC}] is inscribed in the circle, where the side [MATH: \\overline{AB}] is a diameter. Therefore, by Thales' theorem, we have\n[MATH: m\\angle{ACB}=90^\\circ.]\n\nNow, using the fact that [MATH: \\triangle{ABC}] is a right triangle, we obtain\n\n[MATH: m\u2220BAC + m\u2220ABC|= 90^{\u2218}; (2x) + (2x + 10^{\u2218})|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x + 10^{\u2218}|= 90^{\u2218}; 4x|= 80^{\u2218}; x|= 20^{\u2218}.]"
      },
